compare stdout, stderr, and exit code against glink.\n      - id: D3\n        text: Use exec.LookPath(\"glink\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found, following the project differential testing pattern.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/link ./cmd/link/ succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/link/... -count=1 passes all differential tests\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Differential tests verify successful hard link creation with two valid arguments\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/link/ reports no issues\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/link error handling (srd084-link R2.1-R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd084-link.yaml (R2.1-R2.3 error handling requirements)\n      - cmd/link/main.go (existing core implementation from R1.1-R1.4)\n      - cmd/link/link_test.go (existing differential tests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/link/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add error handling for invalid arguments and link failures\n      - path: cmd/link/link_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for error cases\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd084-link R2.1 -- exit with status 1 and print error to stderr when argument count is not exactly 2\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd084-link R2.2 -- exit with status 1 and print error to stderr when the link(2) system call fails\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd084-link R2.3 -- error message format matches GNU link output (e.g., \"link: cannot create link 'target' to 'source': ...\")\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Error messages must match GNU glink format exactly. Run glink with invalid inputs to verify the error prefix and structure.\n      - id: D2\n        text: Reference binary is glink from Homebrew coreutils. Error-case differential tests compare stderr and exit code against glink.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/link ./cmd/link/ succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/link/... -count=1 passes all differential tests including error cases\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Differential tests cover wrong argument count (0, 1, 3+ args), nonexistent source file, and existing target file\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/link/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47065,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":47065},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"322a14ff-c0bb-437b-b806-5af275fa6d13","uuid":"dafc1503-5f91-4066-ad80-e5ba7d1ddd74"}
